---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const principles = [
  ["Make meaning legible", "People should be able to find and understand modeled concepts without reverse-engineering a warehouse dependency graph."],
  ["Separate definitions from questions", "A new analysis should combine stable activities at query time—not require a new tower of intermediate models."],
  ["Make useful work portable", "A common structure makes query patterns, implementation techniques, and analytical methods easier to share."],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mission and creator — Activity Schema"
  description="Why Ahmed Elsamadisi created Activity Schema, how Polyform uses it, and how to join the open community."
  path="/mission/"
>
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">The mission</p>
    <h1>Keep data flexible—and make it explainable.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Activity Schema began with a practical frustration: data teams repeatedly reconstructed the same business concepts in new tables, queries, and reports.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section founder-section">
    <div class="shell founder-grid">
      <div class="founder-meta">
        <span class="mono">Founder note</span>
        <p>Ahmed Elsamadisi<br />Creator of Activity Schema<br />Founder of Polyform</p>
      </div>
      <blockquote>
        <p>“I created Activity Schema because every data question seemed to start by rebuilding the same meaning. I wanted a model that stays close to what actually happened, works as questions change, and is simple enough for a person to explain.”</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell mission-grid">
      {principles.map(([title, description], index) => (
        <article>
          <span class="mono">0{index + 1}</span>
          <h2>{title}</h2>
          <p>{description}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section polyform-section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">From standard to working system</p>
        <h2>Why Ahmed created Polyform.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Activity Schema makes warehouse data easier to model and query. But a trustworthy answer also needs context outside the table: definitions, history, decisions, quality checks, and expert judgment.</p>
        <p>Ahmed created <a href="https://polyform.ai/">Polyform</a> to make that complete loop real. Polyform uses Activity Schema as a shared business-language layer, then combines it with maintained context, live warehouse work, validation, and accountable review. The standard gives the system stable building blocks; the broader system makes sure the work is useful and trustworthy.</p>
        <p>That experience also keeps the standard grounded. Real questions reveal where activity definitions, identity, incremental processing, and human explanation need to become clearer.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="https://polyform.ai/approach/">See how Polyform uses Activity Schema <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section open-section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">An open standard</p>
        <h2>Designed to be used, debated, and improved in public.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Activity Schema 2.0 is published under the Apache 2.0 license. The repository contains the canonical specification, revision history, implementation guidance, and the complete source for this website.</p>
        <p>The standard is independent of any one warehouse, BI tool, company, or AI model.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/ActivitySchema/ActivitySchema">Contribute on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="https://github.com/ActivitySchema/ActivitySchema/blob/main/2.0.md">Read specification 2.0</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section community-section">
    <div class="shell community-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Share your work</p>
        <h2>Doing something useful with Activity Schema?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">Send Ahmed the implementation, tool, article, or experiment. We want this site to show what the community is learning—not only what the specification says.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button button-primary" href="mailto:ahmed@polyform.ai?subject=Activity%20Schema%20project">Email ahmed@polyform.ai <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/global-standard/">Explore the global standard</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .founder-section, .open-section { background: var(--white); }
  .founder-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px minmax(0, 900px); gap: clamp(36px, 8vw, 100px); }
  .founder-meta > span { color: var(--orange); font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .founder-meta p { margin-top: 28px; color: var(--steel); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  blockquote { margin: 0; }
  blockquote p { margin: 0; color: var(--navy); font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 3.7rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.045em; }
  .mission-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .mission-grid article { min-height: 390px; padding: 28px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .mission-grid article:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .mission-grid span { display: block; margin-bottom: 120px; color: var(--seafoam-dark); font-size: 0.68rem; }
  .mission-grid h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem); }
  .mission-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--steel); }
  .split, .community-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(48px, 8vw, 100px); }
  .polyform-section { background: var(--midnight); }
  .polyform-section h2, .polyform-section .eyebrow { color: var(--white); }
  .polyform-section p, .polyform-section a { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); }
  .polyform-section .text-link { color: var(--seafoam-light); }
  .community-section { border-top: 4px solid var(--orange); }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .founder-grid, .split, .community-grid, .mission-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .mission-grid article { min-height: 300px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .mission-grid article:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .mission-grid span { margin-bottom: 70px; }
  }
</style>
